From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: miogds <miogds@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:57:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nsp script: --platform visionos builds a game for Apple
 Vision Pro

The 'ios' build with visionOS libraries and folders of its own:

- the device's shader libraries are compiled through dm/ios/tools/
  xros_metal.py (own_compilers.py for an NVN game, vk_shaders.py or
  gl_shaders.py otherwise) into sh/xros, not sh/ios;
- build_ipa.sh gets DM_SDK=xros and works in ipa-xros, xcode-xros and
  xcode-derived-data-xros;
- the default output is <the profile's IPA>-visionOS.ipa;
- the visionOS SDK is checked with the other prerequisites.

An iPhone build of the same game in the same work folder keeps its
libraries, its project and its IPA. DM_SDK from the shell is not passed
on: the platform is the script's option.

dm/tools/tests/test_nsp_visionos.py: the option, the wrapper only for
visionOS, the output name, and the Vulkan and GL shader steps' command and
folder for both platforms. Not run on a game: there is none here.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: visionOS is outside upstream's support matrix: the NSP script builds a game for it with --platform visionos
Issue: none yet (miogds/NX2Apple, visionOS evaluation branch; to be filed before this goes to LNPANDY/NX2Apple)

